@page "/legal/terms"
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Terms · GymStation</PageTitle>

<main class="legal-shell">
    <header>
        <a class="legal-home" href="/"><BrandMark Size="1.5rem" />GYMSTATION</a>
        <h1>TERMS OF USE</h1>
        <p class="legal-date">EFFECTIVE 2026-08-02</p>
    </header>

    <p>
        These terms cover everyone who signs in to GymStation — gym owners, staff,
        instructors, members, and guardians. Using the platform means you accept them.
    </p>

    <h2>YOUR ACCOUNT</h2>
    <p>Keep your sign-in credentials to yourself. You are responsible for what happens
        under your login. If you think someone else has your password, change it and
        tell your gym.</p>

    <h2>YOUR GYM'S DATA</h2>
    <p>Each gym owns and controls the records it keeps here — its roster, attendance,
        ledger, and published content. GymStation stores those records on the gym's
        behalf. Gyms are responsible for having the authority to enter information about
        the people they add, including minors added under a guardian.</p>

    <h2>PAYMENTS</h2>
    <p>The dues ledger is bookkeeping between you and your gym. GymStation does not
        process card payments and never holds your payment details — how you actually
        pay your gym is between the two of you.</p>

    <h2>ACCEPTABLE USE</h2>
    <p>Don't attempt to access another gym's space or another person's account, probe
        or disrupt the service, or enter data about people you have no authority over.
        Accounts used that way can be suspended.</p>

    <h2>ENDING THINGS</h2>
    <p>Gyms may archive members as part of normal operations. You can stop using the
        platform at any time; your gym handles closing out your record.</p>

    <h2>THE SERVICE ITSELF</h2>
    <p>GymStation is provided as-is, without warranties, to the extent your local law
        allows. We work to keep it accurate and available, but a gym's official records
        — who paid, who was promoted, who attended — are the gym's to certify, not the
        platform's.</p>

    <h2>CHANGES</h2>
    <p>If these terms change, the effective date above changes with them. Continued use
        after a change means you accept the new terms.</p>

    <PlatformFooter />
</main>
